- Cross-model signed log: [Findings](../../model-findings.md)

## Model card

[Primary BF16 card](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-E4B-BF16/raw/main/README.md) and [October 23 launch](https://research.nvidia.com/labs/nemotron/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-E4B-4GB/) establish a Gemma-4-E4B-it-derived, post-trained **8B total / 4B effective** text model under **OpenMDW-1.1**. Effective parameter count does not establish MoE routing. Post-training data cutoff is May 2026. Native **text in/text out**, tools, configurable thinking and concise conversational mode; voice/device use cases rely on adjacent speech/vision components and do not establish native audio/vision input.

Official serving example sets **65,536 shared context tokens**. Card summaries say input/output “up to 64K”; they do not establish a simultaneously usable 128K combined window. The [AA profile](https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/nemotron-3-5-bolt-e4b-4gb) claims image input, 131K context and MoE, but provides no measured intelligence index; primary checkpoint documentation controls these conflicts.

Access: `nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-E4B-BF16` for customization/evaluation; `nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-E4B-4GB` Q4_K_M for local inference; NVIDIA Build `nvidia/nemotron-3.5-bolt-e4b`; local OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions. No verified Zen Free ID or production per-token price found. Open weights are not zero-cost computation. The approximately 4GB footprint refers to quantized target workloads, not BF16 or arbitrary long-context concurrency.

### Raw benchmarks found

NVIDIA's NeMo Gym evaluations, **BF16 / Q4_K_M** respectively:

| Benchmark | BF16 | Q4_K_M |
|---|---:|---:|
| BFCL-v3 | 68.51 | 67.31 |
| Tau2-Bench | 55.10 | 52.32 |
| ToolSandbox | 68.77 | 74.13 |
| When2Call Multi-Turn | 63.36 | 60.50 |
| RelyToolBench | 63.16 | 69.29 |
| MultiChallenge | 53.10 | 55.60 |
| IFBench | 63.79 | 64.00 |
| IHEval | 84.79 | 82.40 |
| AgentIF | 25.81 | 22.95 |
| StructEval-T | 80.40 | 79.99 |
| RULER 64K | 86.99 | 85.76 |
| LongMemEval | 72.10 | 69.92 |
| LongBench v2, 48K | 50.50 | 48.67 |
| GaRAGe | 42.61 | 40.73 |
| RAGTruth F1 | 77.59 | 77.88 |

Reasoning is enabled except RoleBench, EQ-Bench v3 and RULER. BFCL-v3 is not v4; Tau2 aggregate is not Telecom-only or Tau3. When2Call and Brevity benchmarks were not yet publicly released per the launch, reducing reproducibility. [BenchLM's BF16 profile](https://benchlm.ai/models/nemotron-3-5-bolt-e4b-bf16) transcribes publisher results and remains unranked; it is not independent replication.

Publisher Q4_K_M performance: RTX 5070 **3.5GB / 548ms TTFT / 133.4 tokens/s** at batch 1, no cache, 3K input/50 output; **4.3GB / 1,238ms / 106.2 tokens/s** with 32K cache, 2K input/256 output. Do not combine these runtime figures with BF16 quality as one measured deployment.

No verified exact-model SWE-bench, LiveCodeBench, SciCode, Terminal-Bench, GPQA, HLE, CritPt, GDPval-AA or Claw-Eval result recovered. The AA profile's absent index is not a zero. Parent Gemma and larger Bolt 74B scores cannot fill these gaps.

